		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Slowdown with VS 2019]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=42130#p42130"><![CDATA[
Hello,<br><br>I have updated a project by migrating from VS 2017 15.9.12 (tools v141) to VS 2019 16.1.1 (tools v142); almost all function as usual, except when a rigid body collide with a soft body where we have a sudden and huge drop in performances (~75 to ~12 FPS) -- the attached callstack was registered with the 'collision' test scene looping a few times.<br>-When compiled with VS 2017, only a little drop is observed.<br>-The exact same code was compiled (only VS and tools are of different versions).<br><br><strong class="text-strong">Update</strong>: I have narrowed it down to the inlining of functions btSparseSDF::Decompose and btSparseSDF::Lerp; when using __declspec(noinline) to disable their inlining, no performance drop anymore.<br><br>Thank you in advance for your help,<br>Emile<dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=1718" class="postimage" alt="vTune profil VS 2019" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=13297">evignol</a> — Mon May 20, 2019 1:13 pm</p><hr />
